<mujoco model="pick_place_bin_scene">
  <!-- pick_place_scene.xml plus an open container (the bin). Loaded by the bridge only
       when scene.enabled is true; the default scene is loaded from pick_place_scene.xml
       untouched, so with the scene off the simulator is byte-for-byte the legacy one.

       Why a second file instead of a hidden bin inside pick_place_scene.xml: a bin kept
       in the default model but hidden (non-rendered group, no collision) was measured to
       change the RGB image: 5208 of 76800 pixels differ, 5153 of them by one level, 55 by
       up to 86 levels, with depth and every observation bit-identical. The difference
       scales with the hidden geometry's volume (floor 4032, four walls 1300 pixels), does
       not depend on where the bin is, and is the same whether the geoms are hidden by
       group or by alpha=0. A one-millimetre hidden geom or an empty body changed nothing.
       The compile-time statistics (stat.meansize, stat.meanmass) were pinned back to the
       baseline values and that did not remove the difference, so they are not the cause.
       The cause was not found; keeping the bin out of the default model sidesteps it.
       See Job_guides/my_study/week4.1.md Stage 1.

       Static body (no joint): no extra qpos, so the keyframes of the included file stay
       valid, and no TF frame (buildFrameIndex keys off body_jntnum).
       Origin = centre of the inner floor surface; floor 6 mm thick below z=0, walls 6 mm
       thick and 12 mm tall above it. The bridge reads the bin's extent from these geoms
       (scene_ops.cpp readSceneGeometry), so changing the numbers here changes the
       placement checks with them. pos is only the default pose; scene.bin.* moves it. -->
  <include file="pick_place_scene.xml"/>

  <!-- Bin: teal plastic tiles with darker grout lines (Week 5 Stage 8; appearance only). -->
  <asset>
    <texture name="bin_texture" type="2d" builtin="flat" width="64" height="64"
      rgb1="0.15 0.55 0.65" mark="edge" markrgb="0.06 0.30 0.38"/>
    <material name="bin_material" texture="bin_texture" texrepeat="6 6"/>
  </asset>

  <worldbody>
    <body name="bin" pos="0.5 0.3 0.227">
      <geom name="bin_floor" type="box" size="0.076 0.071 0.003" pos="0 0 -0.003"
        material="bin_material"/>
      <geom name="bin_left" type="box" size="0.003 0.071 0.006" pos="-0.073 0 0.006"
        material="bin_material"/>
      <geom name="bin_right" type="box" size="0.003 0.071 0.006" pos="0.073 0 0.006"
        material="bin_material"/>
      <geom name="bin_front" type="box" size="0.07 0.003 0.006" pos="0 -0.068 0.006"
        material="bin_material"/>
      <geom name="bin_back" type="box" size="0.07 0.003 0.006" pos="0 0.068 0.006"
        material="bin_material"/>
    </body>
  </worldbody>
</mujoco>
